# negative seed.
#
# Scenario: a capability cell `Softmax` is declared with a `class:` whose
# token is outside the closed taxonomy. A compiler that silently admits it
# would mint a CellId over an unbounded class and later branch on an
# invented name.
#
# expect: E-CELL-001 - typed refusal at the emath-ir admission seam
# (emath_ir::admit_cell), never silent identity over an unknown class.
use std.kinds.capability

emath capability Softmax:
    class: transcendental-quick
    version: 1.0.0
    migration: bump-and-note "initial"
    inputs:
        x: Float64
    outputs:
        value: Float64
    definitions:
        value = exp(x) / sum i in 0..3: exp(x)
